(1001, 'competent', 'adjective', 'c1', '7.0 - 8.0+', '/ˈkɒmpɪtənt/', '/ˈkɑːmpɪtənt/', '( competent as / at / in something ) ( competent to do something ) thạo, rành', 'having enough skill or knowledge to do something well or to the necessary standard', 'He''s very competent in his work.', 'Anh ấy rất có năng lực trong công việc của mình.', ARRAY['competent in his work', 'competent in']::text[], ARRAY['skilled', 'capable', 'proficient']::text[], ARRAY['incompetent']::text[], '{"noun": "companion", "verb": "compare", "adverb": "completely"}'::jsonb, 'competent_uk.mp3', 'competent_us.mp3', 'Academic, Research & Abstract Concepts', 'Abstract Ideas & Theories'),
